---
/**
 * hospitality / PageBJ — "Kubo Stays" (rooms for rent in an owner-hosted house).
 *
 * Cream & deep green: Instrument Serif display over DM Sans body on a warm
 * cream ground, with a terracotta eyebrow and two full-bleed green bands. The
 * signature of the design is the ITALIC SERIF EMPHASIS inside a headline — the
 * hero's last line, and any <em> an owner types into a section h2.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet boot, skip link, scroll-reveal). It does NOT compose
 * with BaseLayout. It is the only file in the variant that touches `siteData`;
 * the 15 section components receive only `layout` + `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. PageBJ renders no editable text of
 * its own — it only READS layout.businessName / layout.tagline (<title>),
 * content.description (<meta name="description">), layout.favicon (<link
 * rel="icon">) and layout.ogImage || layout.favicon (og:image). Every
 * data-field / data-image-field / data-href-field hook lives in a section
 * component. Section visibility is the 13 camelCase `visibility.*` keys below,
 * every one tested `!== false` (undefined ⇒ render).
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING in the whole template is the skip link's
 * "Skip to content" below. It is an a11y affordance, visible on focus only, and
 * it matches PageBI. Flagged here so it reads as a decision, not an oversight.
 *
 * PROP PLUMBING: every section is handed BOTH `content` and `layout`, even the
 * ones whose contract lists only content.* keys. Extra props are inert in
 * Astro, whereas a section that reaches for layout.contact.phone with no
 * `layout` prop throws at build. This variant was authored in parallel, so the
 * uniform call is the safe one.
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block is prefixed
 * `html[data-page="BJ"]`, including the `*` reset, `body`, `img`, `a`,
 * `::selection` and the base primitives, so nothing leaks into a sister wrapper
 * built in the same run — and nothing leaks in.
 *
 * THEMING: the native palette is emitted FIRST and the engine's
 * `html:root{…!important}` block LAST in <head>, which is the only reason an
 * explicit admin colour pick wins the cascade. Never move it above the design's
 * global style block or above the {__fontHref} link.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (two lines, wrapper-local, touches no shared file):
 * lib/astro-builder.ts defaults `layout.fontPairing` to the literal 'modern',
 * and resolveTheme's `lockVariant` only blanks ''/'auto'/'default' — so without
 * the sentinel buildOverrideCss force-swaps Space Grotesk + Inter with
 * !important on ~every real site and Instrument Serif never reaches a visitor.
 * We treat astro-builder's DEFAULT as unset; a deliberate admin pick still
 * applies.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES in this template (read lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts
 * before adding a button anywhere):
 *   .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right
 *   .testi .cta-band .trust, and `.hero` on a <section>.
 * Note .trust and .cta-band are forbidden HERE although PageBI uses both: the
 * engine pins `.trust{color:<on-ink>}` and `.cta-band .btn{color:<on-ink>}`,
 * which is correct only for an element sitting on an INK fill. BJ's proof band
 * sits on the light --paper-2 tint (class .proof) and BJ's closing band carries
 * a PAPER-filled button (class .closing), so both pins would strand a label.
 * Buttons here are .btn--fill / .btn--line / .linkc (double dash) — they dodge
 * the engine's `.btn-primary{color:<on-primary>!important}` pin, which is
 * sub-AA in 6 of 13 schemes.
 *
 * PALETTE DEVIATIONS FROM THE DESIGN, all deliberate:
 *  (a) --ink is the design's DEEP GREEN #143F38, not its near-black #17140F.
 *      The green bands (How, the whole-house slab, the closing band) must be
 *      painted with var(--ink) on var(--paper): buildOverrideCss remaps
 *      --accent-deep to palette.primaryDeep, which is #FFFFFF in the 'dark'
 *      scheme and #E5E5E5 in 'black' — both allowed for this family — so a
 *      green band built on --accent-deep would render white-on-white. The
 *      ink/paper pair is the only pairing legible in all 13 schemes, in both
 *      directions.
 *  (b) --accent is a DARKENED terracotta #A9501F (5.06:1 on cream) rather than
 *      the design's #C4622D (3.83:1): the eyebrows are 10px caps and must
 *      clear AA.
 *  (c) --muted is #6E6759 (5.20:1 on cream, 4.81 on the tint) rather than the
 *      design's label grey #8C8578, which measures 3.40:1 on cream and fails
 *      AA for the 10–12px text it is used on. It sits between the design's own
 *      two greys (#5C554B body, #8C8578 label) and reads as the same stone.
 *  (d) The headline <em> is ITALIC ONLY, with `color: inherit`. The design
 *      tints it green against a near-black headline; here the headline is
 *      already that green, and the obvious substitute — var(--accent) — is
 *      1.72:1 against the maroon scheme's paper, which would delete a word
 *      from the middle of a sentence. The italic serif IS the signature.
 *  GOLD (--accent-light) IS DECORATION ONLY: never a button fill, never body
 *  text, never an eyebrow on an inverted band. The engine remaps it to
 *  palette.accent (#A52A2A maroon, #A0A0A0 dark/black), so gold-on-green would
 *  become maroon-on-ink. It is confined to aria-hidden numerals and hairlines.
 *
 * KNOWN RISK, recorded not fixed: the eyebrow (.kick) is var(--accent) per the
 * contract's palette decision. Native cream that is 5.06:1, but the engine
 * remaps --accent to palette.primary, which is #800000 on the maroon scheme's
 * #2D0000 paper = 1.72:1. Every eyebrow in the template is decorative-adjacent
 * (the h2 beneath always repeats the section's meaning), so a dimmed eyebrow
 * degrades rather than breaks — but the honest fix is a shared-file change to
 * the maroon palette, which is out of scope here.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER: Header, Hero, Trust, Services (the rooms), Why (the house),
 * Gallery, About (your host), Credentials (the promises), How, Testimonials,
 * Area, Location, Faq, CtaBand, Footer. Rooms lead, because on this vertical
 * the rate and the room are the product. Credentials sits immediately after
 * About on purpose: the design nests the promise cards in the host section's
 * right column, and one content prefix per <section> forbids that — see
 * CredentialsBJ.
 *
 * INVERTED BANDS: a section that wants the green ground carries BOTH its own
 * name and `band-shade` (e.g. class="closing band-shade"), exactly as PageBI's
 * footer does. That one class flips the h2, body, eyebrow, chip, hairline and
 * button treatments in this file; a section should not restate them.
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper defines window.__hospitalityBJInitMap (family-unique)
 * and LocationBJ calls that exact string. Keep `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot —
 * it is what erases the drawn fallback map-face — and keep id="map" literal.
 */
import HeaderBJ from './header/HeaderBJ.astro';
import HeroBJ from './hero/HeroBJ.astro';
import TrustBJ from './trust/TrustBJ.astro';
import ServicesBJ from './services/ServicesBJ.astro';
import WhyBJ from './why/WhyBJ.astro';
import GalleryBJ from './gallery/GalleryBJ.astro';
import AboutBJ from './about/AboutBJ.astro';
import CredentialsBJ from './credentials/CredentialsBJ.astro';
import HowBJ from './how/HowBJ.astro';
import TestimonialsBJ from './testimonials/TestimonialsBJ.astro';
import AreaBJ from './area/AreaBJ.astro';
import LocationBJ from './location/LocationBJ.astro';
import FaqBJ from './faq/FaqBJ.astro';
import CtaBandBJ from './ctaBand/CtaBandBJ.astro';
import FooterBJ from './footer/FooterBJ.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice (lib/astro-builder.ts).
// Treating it as unset keeps Instrument Serif; a deliberate admin pick applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BJ">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A <meta> cannot read a CSS var, so this duplicates
       the cream ground token (--paper) that the sticky header sits on. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#FAF6F0" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- Kubo Stays native fonts, taken verbatim from the design: Instrument Serif
       with BOTH italic axes (the italic is the template's signature, so it must
       be a real cut and never a synthesised oblique) plus DM Sans for body and
       labels. Always loaded so the variant reads as designed even when the
       admin never touched the font dropdown. -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,300;9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {(layout.ogImage || layout.favicon) && <meta property="og:image" content={layout.ogImage || layout.favicon} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBJ · "Kubo Stays" — hospitality (rooms for rent, owner-hosted).
       Tokens + shared base primitives. EVERY selector is prefixed
       html[data-page="BJ"] so nothing leaks into a sister wrapper, or in.

       FIVE LOAD-BEARING FACTS. Do not "tidy" any of them:

       1. SPECIFICITY. Every appearance-bearing base primitive is wrapped in
          :where() -> (0,1,1), so an Astro-scoped single-compound section rule
          (0,2,0) wins. Removing a :where() is the documented cause of every
          photo frame collapsing to the base height (squished band). BELT AND
          BRACES: sections also size .plate with an INLINE
          style="aspect-ratio:X;min-height:0" — inline outranks every selector,
          so the specificity argument never has to be won per section.

       2. BUTTON CLASS NAMES. .btn--fill / .btn--line / .linkc, double-dash, on
          purpose. They dodge buildOverrideCss's
          `.btn-primary,…{color:<on-primary>!important}` (sub-AA in 6 of 13
          schemes) and `.hero .btn-ghost{…!important}` (which would strand a
          white label on this cream hero — the arrival section is class
          "arrival", never "hero"). NEVER use in this template:
          .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right
          .testi .cta-band .trust. The proof band is .proof and the closing band
          is .closing precisely so the engine's on-ink pins cannot reach them —
          BJ's proof band sits on a LIGHT tint and BJ's closing band carries a
          PAPER-filled button, so both pins would be wrong. There is ZERO
          !important in this template outside the reduced-motion reveal reset.

       3. HOVER. Never changes hue, never goes light or transparent. An inset
          rgba(0,0,0,.16) darkens only the fill (it paints above the background
          and below the label), so a label can never strand mid-transition.

       4. FOCUS. One DUO ring for everything: a 3px var(--paper) outline inside
          a 6px var(--ink) halo. Built from the ink/paper pair, so on cream the
          ink halo separates the ring from the page and on a green band the
          paper ring separates from the halo — the same pair, both directions,
          in all 13 schemes.

       5. HEAD ORDER. This block must be followed by
          {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />} and then,
          as the LAST node in the head, a global style node fed
          set:html={__overrideCss}. The engine's html:root{…!important} only
          beats these tokens because it comes later in source order.
          (Never write a literal closing style or script tag inside this block,
          comments included — it is an HTML raw-text element, so the parser
          would end the stylesheet right there.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BJ"] {
      /* grounds — cream / oatmeal tint / white card */
      --paper: #FAF6F0;
      --paper-2: #F3EDE2;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      /* ink — the design's DEEP GREEN. Both a text colour and the ground of
         every inverted band. See PALETTE DEVIATION (a). */
      --ink: #143F38;
      --ink-soft: #4C5F57;
      --line: #E6DED1;
      /* warmth — darkened terracotta primary, forest deep, gold decoration */
      --accent: #A9501F;
      --accent-deep: #0F2E29;
      --accent-light: #E0A63A;
      --muted: #6E6759;
      /* rgb triplets for token-driven tints (all remapped by buildOverrideCss) */
      --paper-rgb: 250,246,240;
      --ink-rgb: 20,63,56;
      --accent-rgb: 169,80,31;
      /* contrast aliases the override engine + inherited rules expect */
      --on-ink: #FAF6F0;
      --on-paper: #143F38;
      --on-accent: #FFFFFF;
      --on-primary: #FFFFFF;
      /* type + metrics */
      --disp: "Instrument Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --serif: "Instrument Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --sans: "DM Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      /* This design has no monospace: its small caps labels are DM Sans. The
         token exists because the engine sets it and shared primitives read it. */
      --mono: "DM Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --maxw: 1240px;
      --r-lg: 20px;
      --r-md: 18px;
      --r-sm: 12px;
    }

    /* VERIFIED CONTRAST (sRGB relative luminance, native palette):
       ink/paper 10.85 · ink/paper-2 10.03 · ink/card 11.68
       ink-soft/paper 6.33 · /paper-2 5.85 · /card 6.81
       muted/paper 5.20 · /paper-2 4.81 · /card 5.60
       accent/paper 5.06 (eyebrows, 10px caps) · accent/card 5.45
       paper on ink 10.85 · rgba(paper,.86) 8.9 · .78 7.6 · .62 5.1
       BANNED, recorded as evidence: design terracotta #C4622D/paper 3.83 ·
       design label grey #8C8578/paper 3.40 · gold #E0A63A as text on cream 1.87 ·
       engine --accent-deep (#FFFFFF) as a band ground on the dark scheme 1.00 ·
       engine --accent as text on the maroon scheme's paper 1.72.
       WORST OF THE 6 SCHEMES THIS FAMILY ALLOWS: ink/paper 9.11 (maroon) ·
       our paper label on a 16%-darkened ink fill 10.0+ everywhere. Nothing
       carrying text is below 4.5:1 except the eyebrow under a remap — see the
       KNOWN RISK note in the frontmatter. */

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BJ"] *,
    html[data-page="BJ"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BJ"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BJ"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BJ"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.7;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] ::selection { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink);
      letter-spacing: 0; line-height: 1.06;
    }
    /* This bare-element paragraph reset is (0,1,1): always qualify a section's
       own paragraph rules with a parent class (.host-prose p) so they win. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(p) { margin: 0 0 1em; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.wrap) { width: min(var(--maxw), 92vw); margin-inline: auto; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] section { padding: clamp(60px,8vw,92px) 0; position: relative; }

    /* ── BAND GROUNDS. Three, and only three. Sections pick one by name.
          Default (no class) = cream --paper. A section wanting the green ground
          carries `band-shade` ALONGSIDE its own class name. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-tint) { background-color: var(--paper-2); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-card) { background-color: var(--card); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) { background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .h2,
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .fig { color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .body,
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .lede { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.78); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .mono { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.74); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .plate { border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.18); }

    /* ── .kick — the eyebrow. 10px caps, wide tracking, terracotta. On an
          inverted band it becomes paper-derived: the design's gold eyebrow is
          NOT portable (the engine turns gold into #A52A2A on maroon and
          #A0A0A0 on dark), and gold is decoration only in this template. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.kick) {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .4em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .kick { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.82); }

    /* ── display headline + the ITALIC SERIF EMPHASIS (the design's signature).
          <em> is ITALIC ONLY and keeps `inherit` — see PALETTE DEVIATION (d).
          Sections feed the h2 with set:html so an owner can place the emphasis
          anywhere in their own sentence. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.h2) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400;
      font-size: clamp(30px,4.3vw,56px); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: 0;
      margin: 0 0 .3em; color: var(--ink); max-width: 22ch;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.h2 em),
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.h2 .em),
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.em) { font-style: italic; color: inherit; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.lede) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(15.5px,1.5vw,17.5px); line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 46ch; margin: 0;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.body) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(14.5px,1.3vw,15.5px); line-height: 1.7;
    }
    /* ── .mono — small tracked caps on a light ground (--muted, 4.81 worst) */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.mono) {
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    }
    /* ── .fig — the serif money/stat figure. tabular-nums survives a font swap. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.fig) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums; line-height: 1;
    }

    /* ── BUTTONS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Proven pairs (native / worst of the 6 schemes this family allows):
         .btn--fill            paper on ink                 10.85 / 9.11
         .btn--fill:hover      paper on ink+16% black        12.4 / 10.3
         .btn--line            ink on card                   11.68 / 9.4
         .btn--line:hover      paper on ink                  10.85 / 9.11
         .band-shade .btn--fill  ink on paper                10.85 / 9.11
         .band-shade .btn--line  paper on ink                10.85 / 9.11
         .linkc                ink on cream (never changes on hover) 10.85 / 9.11
       No fill is EVER a mid-tone: every one is the darkest or the lightest
       token of the pair. The design's terracotta-filled pill is deliberately
       NOT reproduced — an --accent fill under a --paper label measures 1.72:1
       on the maroon scheme, where both tokens collapse into the same red. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .55em;
      padding: 16px 30px; min-height: 48px;
      border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid transparent;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
      transition: background-color .18s ease, box-shadow .18s ease, transform .18s ease, border-color .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn--fill) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 999px rgba(0,0,0,.16), 0 0 0 4px rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.28);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn--fill:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* The design's secondary pill: a white card fill inside a hairline. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn--line) {
      background-color: var(--card); color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--line);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn--line:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* INSIDE a green band both variants invert. Declared once, globally, so no
       section has to restate them — and so no section is tempted to invent a
       gold fill, which the engine would turn into maroon-on-ink. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .btn--fill {
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--paper);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .btn--fill:hover {
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--paper);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 999px rgba(0,0,0,.16), 0 0 0 4px rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.24);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .btn--line {
      background-color: transparent; color: var(--paper); border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.45);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .btn--line:hover {
      background-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.14); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--paper);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BJ"] .btn { transition: none; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] .btn--fill:hover,
      html[data-page="BJ"] .btn--line:hover { transform: none; }
    }

    /* ── .linkc — quiet text-link action. Used INSTEAD of a second button in the
          footer and inside any band the engine pins, because it carries no .btn
          class. Its colour never changes on hover (only the rule under it
          thickens), so it cannot fail a contrast check mid-interaction. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5em; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px;
      letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--ink);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-bottom: 2px;
      transition: border-bottom-width .18s ease, border-bottom-color .18s ease, transform .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.linkc:hover) {
      color: var(--ink); border-bottom-width: 3px; border-bottom-color: var(--ink);
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .linkc { color: var(--paper); border-bottom-color: var(--accent-light); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BJ"] .linkc { transition: none; } }

    /* ── FOCUS · the DUO ring. See load-bearing fact 4. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--ink);
      border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn):focus-visible,
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.linkc):focus-visible { border-radius: 999px; }

    /* ── .plate — THE photo frame. Every image in the template is one of these.
          Sections size it with an inline style="aspect-ratio:X;min-height:0".
          The fallback face is token-built, so it recolours with the scheme —
          and a section must OMIT the plate entirely when the owner supplied no
          photo rather than ship a decorative empty box. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.plate) {
      position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-radius: var(--r-lg);
      background-color: var(--paper-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); isolation: isolate;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.plate) .ph {
      position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1;
      background-color: var(--paper-2);
      background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(78% 64% at 22% 14%, rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.22), transparent 62%),
        radial-gradient(66% 60% at 84% 90%, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.22), transparent 60%);
      transition: transform .5s ease;
    }
    /* .cap — caption on an OPAQUE ink pill, never a gradient scrim: 10.85 over
       ANY owner photo, however dark or blown out. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.plate) .cap {
      position: absolute; left: 12px; bottom: 12px; z-index: 3;
      max-width: calc(100% - 24px);
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px;
      letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 6px 11px; border-radius: 999px;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.plate) .ph { transition: none; } }

    /* ── .chip — the design's outline pill (room features, footer channels).
          Hairline border, ink-soft label, no fill: an accent-TINTED chip would
          go invisible under the dark and black schemes, where --accent-rgb is
          a mid grey. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.chip) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
      background-color: transparent; color: var(--ink-soft);
      border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 6px 12px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 500; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .chip {
      color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.86); border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.30);
    }

    /* ── .rowrule — the one hairline row separator used by every list/ledger in
          the template (amenities, house rules, FAQ). Per-cell border, never a
          gap-over-inked-container trick: that paints a visible block in the
          EMPTY tracks of a partial last row. */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.rowrule) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.band-shade) .rowrule { border-bottom-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.20); }

    /* ── scroll reveal (the boot IIFE at the end of the body toggles .in) ── */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.reveal) { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px); transition: opacity .7s ease, transform .7s ease; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.reveal.in) { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="1"]) { transition-delay: .08s; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="2"]) { transition-delay: .16s; }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="3"]) { transition-delay: .24s; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BJ"] .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    }

    /* ── skip link ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 0 0 var(--r-sm) 0;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }

    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 760px ───────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      html[data-page="BJ"] section { padding: clamp(48px,10vw,72px) 0; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.wrap) { width: min(var(--maxw), 90vw); }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(27px,7.2vw,42px); max-width: none; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.lede) { max-width: none; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.plate) { border-radius: var(--r-md); }
    }

    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 520px (verified no horizontal overflow at 360px) ── */
    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      html[data-page="BJ"] body { font-size: 16px; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(25px,8vw,32px); }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.kick) { font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: .26em; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.mono) { letter-spacing: .14em; }
      html[data-page="BJ"] :where(.btn) { padding: 15px 22px; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .12em; white-space: normal; text-align: center; flex: 1 1 100%; }
    }
  </style>

  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBJ layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {/* Rooms → the house → gallery lead, BEFORE the story: on this vertical the
        rate and the room are the product. Deliberate; do not reorder. */}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {/* The promise cards sit immediately under the host block, on the same
        ground and with no top rule, so the two read as one spread — the design
        nests them in the host section's right column, which one-content-prefix-
        per-section forbids. */}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBJ content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBJ layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      if (!reduce && !document.hidden) {
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (es) {
          es.forEach(function (e) { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); } });
        }, { threshold: 0.1, rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px' });
        document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { io.observe(el); });
      } else {
        document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { el.classList.add('in'); });
      }
      // Kubo Stays / BJ Leaflet boot — accepts (lat, lng, label) from LocationBJ.
      // The global name is family-unique on purpose: a preview harness can render
      // two wrappers in one document, and a shared name cross-wires the maps.
      window.__hospitalityBJInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
        if (!window.L) return;
        var el = document.getElementById('map'); if (!el) return;
        // Erases LocationBJ's drawn fallback map-face; without this the tiles
        // stack on top of the drawn grid.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = L.map('map', { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 15);
        // LABELLED basemap: a guest orienting to a barangay, pier or highway
        // needs place names, so this family uses CARTO voyager, not nolabels.
        L.tileLayer('https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO', maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd' }).addTo(map);
        // Marker colours are READ from the live tokens rather than baked, so an
        // explicit admin colour pick recolours the pin too (buildOverrideCss sets
        // them on html:root, which is this same element).
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#A9501F';
        var paper = (cs.getPropertyValue('--paper') || '').trim() || '#FAF6F0';
        var icon = L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:50%;background:' + accent + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 3px ' + paper + ';border:0;"></div>',
          iconSize: [14, 14], iconAnchor: [7, 7]
        });
        L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon }).addTo(map).bindPopup('<b>' + label + '</b>');
      };
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
